The packaged extension (.vsix) bundles the tizen-sdk-skills runtime under
dist/assets/ and therefore redistributes the following third-party material:

1. tizen-dlog-analyzer prebuilt binaries
   dist/assets/tools/tizen-dlog-analyzer/{linux,windows}/
   PyInstaller bundles of the Tizen DLog Analyzer (Apache-2.0, Samsung Electronics)
   embedding CPython, OpenSSL, zlib, bzip2, xz, Expat, libffi, libuuid, pydantic,
   typer, click, rich, Pygments, colorama and others. The component list, licenses
   and SHA-256 checksums are in dist/assets/tools/tizen-dlog-analyzer/NOTICE.md.

2. Samsung TV developer CA certificates
   dist/assets/assets/samsung-tv-ca/vd_tizen_dev_author_ca.cer
   dist/assets/assets/samsung-tv-ca/vd_tizen_dev_partner2.crt
   dist/assets/assets/samsung-tv-ca/vd_tizen_dev_public2.crt
   Public CA certificates (no private keys) as distributed with the Samsung TV SDK
   extension, used by the certificate manager to build TV signing profiles.
   Copyright Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd.

3. Tizen project templates
   dist/assets/scripts/tizen-create-project/templates/{native,web,dotnet,platform}/
   Derived from the sample project templates shipped with Tizen Studio and the
   Tizen DALi demo (https://www.tizen.org), used to scaffold new user projects.
   The DALi demo packaging spec declares Apache-2.0; the remaining template
   files carry no per-file license header and are redistributed here under
   Apache-2.0.

4. Runtime dependencies
   The extension bundle (dist/extension.js) is produced by esbuild from the
   dependencies declared in package.json, each under the license recorded in
   the npm registry.

